{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable\/Mockable()"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:8MockableAAyycfm","title":"Mockable()","symbolKind":"macro","roleHeading":"Macro","modules":[{"name":"Mockable"}],"fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Mockable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"A peer macro that generates a mock implementation for the protocol it is attached to.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(peer, names: prefixed(Mock)) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Mockable"},{"kind":"text","text":"()"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generated implementation is named with a “Mock” prefix followed by the protocol name.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the generated code is enclosed in an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#if MOCKING"},{"text":" condition, ensuring it is only accessible","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in modules where the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MOCKING"},{"text":" compile-time condition is set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Example usage:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Mockable","protocol UserService {","    func get(id: UUID) -> User","    func remove(id: UUID) throws","}","","var mockUserService: MockUserService","","func test() {","    let error: UserError = .invalidId","    let mockUser = User(id: UUID())","","    given(mockUserService)","        .get(id: .any).willReturn(mockUser)","        .remove(id: .any).willThrow(error)","","    try await loginService.login()","","    verify(mockUserService)","        .get(id: .value(mockUser.id)).called(count: .once)","        .remove(id: .any).called(count: .never)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mockable\/mockable()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Mockable/documentation/Mockable/Mockable()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable\/Mockable()","abstract":[{"text":"A peer macro that generates a mock implementation for the protocol it is attached to.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/mockable\/mockable()","title":"Mockable()","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Mockable","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Mockable/documentation/Mockable":{"role":"collection","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Mockable\/documentation\/Mockable","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/mockable","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro driven testing framework that provides automatic mock implementations for your protocols. It offers an intuitive declarative syntax that simplifies the process of mocking services in unit tests."}],"title":"Mockable"}}}